negatively oriented if it is traversed clockwise.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the curves:\n\n- Curve I is not closed.\n\n- Curve II is simple, closed, negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed clockwise.\n\n- Curve III is a simple and closed curve but it is not negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed counterclockwise, so it is positively oriented.\n\n- Curve IV is not simple.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is curve II only"] [:db/cas 17592186470557 :answer-field/key "I" "![Curve I](images/91/9183ef08d96d4d5278f24375c1977aaf601bc6eaf4748bb5ab6ba686b295cb04.svg)"] [:db/cas 17592186470558 :answer-field/key "II" "![Curve II](images/d1/d13722546fd99577ae33f47d18a9ed106d6fb28277051cef824c27e46a4ac970.svg)"] [:db/cas 17592186470559 :answer-field/key "III" "![Curve III](images/6f/6f2b89368f7018dff9c5a857d41856679fe6706350d605eac799f06d8f9a95d2.svg)"] [:db/cas 17592186470560 :answer-field/key "IV" "![Curve IV](images/5c/5c5907733fdb9a4c6b6f876dd2abb0528240b2a50c0037f67d240dadfaf3e791.svg)"] [:db/cas 17592186362310 :question/problem "![](images/0d/0db1568fab302ddbd9f16dbdf9c276eeb62cbac37346b077c1639fe68c2396ac.png)\n\nWhich of the regions shown above are simply connected?\n\nSelect all that apply." "Which of the regions shown below are simply connected?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186362310 :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\n